{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/676027-relationships-between-hunters-and-mortals","id":676027,"title":"Relationships between Hunters and Mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T22:26:47-07:00","id":676027,"title":"Relationships between Hunters and Mortals","content":"Okay, I've been away for a while and need a warm-up pitch. Let's talk relationships that hunters have with the people in their lives. When do you think a hunter decides to tell someone the truth, or decides who gets to keep the reality buried beneath every imaginable lie available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T16:19:46-07:00","id":677005,"title":"","content":"It depends on a lot of factors, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> First of all, there's the optimism vs cynicism factor: does the Hunter believe that the person they want to reveal themselves to will actually listen to them and believe them? Remember, in NWoD, the Masquerade isn't so much &quot;mortals don't know the supernatural exists&quot; as it is &quot;mortals <i>don't want to <b>think</b></i> about the supernatural existing&quot;. A lot of people won't listen to a Hunter who tries to clue them in because they don't want to think about it. Everyone has some sneaking suspicion about things going bump in the night, but nobody wants to be seen as &quot;crazy&quot; for daring to bump back.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there's the paranoia factor: does the Hunter trust this person will not endanger either themselves or the Hunter with this information? Let's face it, do you really want to tell your goth daughter what <b>real</b> vampires are like if there's an actual chance she'll go after them willingly, because she doesn't accept your stories that they're monsters?<br /> <br /> With these two factors, most Hunters choose to leave other people in the dark - it's futile more often than not, and too dangerous in either case. It's part of the reason Hunters form Cells and have their own forums and the like; it's not just about tactics, it's about the sheer stress relief of having <i>people who know</i> to talk to.<br /> <br /> Hunters aren't that different from the supernaturals in a lot of ways. First and foremost, their exposure to the dark underbelly of reality cuts them off from any significant interactions with baseline humans. They can fake living in the mortal's world enough to fool themselves, but really, they are inherently set apart by the knowledge (and powers, for Tier 3 hunters) that they bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}